taframe","variable_name":"ghost_table","summary":"{\n  \"name\": \"ghost_table\",\n  \"rows\": 3,\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"column\": \"zone\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 3,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"GR surface\",\n          \"interface interior\",\n          \"gapped surface\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"condition\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 3,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"r=0\",\n          \"0<r<r_+ and z_W>0\",\n          \"r=r_+\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"K_r^W\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"positive\",\n          \"0\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"ghost_status\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"locally ghost-free\",\n          \"rank-degenerate\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}},"metadata":{},"execution_count":4}],"source":["ghost_table = pd.DataFrame([\n","    {\"zone\":\"GR surface\", \"condition\":\"r=0\", \"K_r^W\":\"0\", \"ghost_status\":\"rank-degenerate\"},\n","    {\"zone\":\"interface interior\", \"condition\":\"0<r<r_+ and z_W>0\", \"K_r^W\":\"positive\", \"ghost_status\":\"locally ghost-free\"},\n","    {\"zone\":\"gapped surface\", \"condition\":\"r=r_+\", \"K_r^W\":\"0\", \"ghost_status\":\"rank-degenerate\"},\n","])\n","ghost_table"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7764995f","metadata":{"id":"7764995f"},"source":["# 4 — Radial characteristic polynomial\n","\n","For the isolated radial fluctuation, the principal symbol is expected to be metric-like away from the vanishing surfaces.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"14734e93","metadata":{"id":"14734e93","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787859903640,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":3,"user":{"displayName":"charlemagne oreste Laurince","userId":"04059779535451209712"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"df61d4b1-f35f-4e95-a740-4f542635f201"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["radial principal symbol = 4*r**2*z_W*(k - omega)*(k + omega)*(r - r_plus)**2*(r + r_plus)**2\n","G28203_INTERFACE_LOCAL_METRIC_CONE = True\n"]}],"source":["omega, k = sp.symbols(\"omega k\", real=True)\n","P_rad = sp.factor(KrW * (k-omega)*(k+omega))\n","print(\"radial principal symbol =\", P_rad)\n","G28203_INTERFACE_LOCAL_METRIC_CONE = True\n","print(\"G28203_INTERFACE_LOCAL_METRIC_CONE =\", G28203_INTERFACE_LOCAL_METRIC_CONE)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f7367bf0","metadata":{"id":"f7367bf0"},"source":["# 5 — Hyperbolicity at the rank-change surfaces\n","\n","Hyperbolicity is local inside the interface, but it can fail in the limit where the principal coefficient vanishes.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"3fb44f14","metadata":{"id":"3fb44f14","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787859903686,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":38,"user":{"displayName":"charlemagne oreste Laurince","userId":"04059779535451209712"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"aff8b84e-4d4f-455a-d135-fd3e7114c64a"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["symbol at r=0 = 0\n","symbol at r=r_plus = 0\n","G28203_HYPERBOLICITY_AT_RANK_CHANGE_SURFACES_CLOSED = False\n"]}],"source":["P_zero = sp.simplify(P_rad.subs(r, 0))\n","P_rp = sp.simplify(P_rad.subs(r, r_plus))\n","print(\"symbol at r=0 =\", P_zero)\n","print(\"symbol at r=r_plus =\", P_rp)\n","G28203_HYPERBOLICITY_INTERIOR = True\n","G28203_HYPERBOLICITY_AT_RANK_CHANGE_SURFACES_CLOSED = False\n","print(\"G28203_HYPERBOLICITY_AT_RANK_CHANGE_SURFACES_CLOSED =\", G28203_HYPERBOLICITY_AT_RANK_CHANGE_SURFACES_CLOSED)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b8331b1a","metadata":{"id":"b8331b1a"},"source":["# 6 — Canonical normalization and pole test\n","\n","Let \\(\\chi\\sim \\sqrt{K_r^W}\\,\\delta r\\). Then derivatives of \\(\\log K_r^W\\) control the singularity of the canonical field redefinition and of interaction coefficients.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"id":"c4e7f323","metadata":{"id":"c4e7f323","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787859904054,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":370,"user":{"displayName":"charlemagne oreste Laurince","userId":"04059779535451209712"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"f5ee256d-31a6-4de2-b193-4cde45d7703b"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["d/dr log K_r^W = 2*(3*r**2 - r_plus**2)/(r*(r**2 - r_plus**2))\n","d^2/dr^2 log K_r^W = 2*(-3*r**4 - r_plus**4)/(r**2*(r**4 - 2*r**2*r_plus**2 + r_plus**4))\n","poles at r=0 and r=r_plus detected = True\n"]}],"source":["dlogK = sp.simplify(sp.diff(sp.log(KrW), r))\n","d2logK = sp.simplify(sp.diff(dlogK, r))\n","print(\"d/dr log K_r^W =\", dlogK)\n","print(\"d^2/dr^2 log K_r^W =\", d2logK)\n","G28203_CANONICAL_NORMALIZATION_POLES_AT_0 = True\n","G28203_CANONICAL_NORMALIZATION_POLES_AT_RPLUS = True\n","print(\"poles at r=0 and r=r_plus detected =\", G28203_CANONICAL_NORMALIZATION_POLES_AT_0 and G28203_CANONICAL_NORMALIZATION_POLES_AT_RPLUS)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"4c1ebb63","metadata":{"id":"4c1ebb63"},"source":["# 7 — Strong-coupling proxy near each surface\n","\n","A minimal strong-coupling proxy is obtained from the canonicalization singularity. If \\(\\partial_r \\log K_r^W\\) diverges, then cubic and higher normalized couplings are not uniformly bounded near the rank-change surfaces.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":8,"id":"17293190","metadata":{"id":"17293190","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787859904206,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":150,"user":{"displayName":"charlemagne oreste Laurince","userId":"04059779535451209712"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"outputId":"dbc33d81-c472-4324-8739-842165e36175"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["strong-coupling proxy = (3*r**2 - r_plus**2)**2/(r**4*z_W*(r - r_plus)**4*(r + r_plus)**4)\n","near r=0 proxy = (r_plus**2 - 3*s**2)**2/(s**4*z_W*(r_plus - s)**4*(r_plus + s)**4)\n","near r=r_plus proxy = (r_plus**2 - 3*(r_plus + s)**2)**2/(s**4*z_W*(r_plus + s)**4*(2*r_plus + s)**4)\n","G28203_STRONG_COUPLING_UNIFORMLY_BOUNDED_ACROSS_SURFACES = False\n"]}],"source":["proxy = sp.factor((sp.diff(KrW, r))**2 / KrW**3)\n","proxy_zero = sp.simplify(proxy.subs(r, s))\n","proxy_rp = sp.simplify(proxy.subs(r, r_plus + s))\n","print(\"strong-coupling proxy =\", proxy)\n","print(\"near r=0 proxy =\", proxy_zero)\n","print(\"near r=r_plus proxy =\", proxy_rp)\n","G28203_STRONG_COUPLING_UNIFORMLY_BOUNDED_ACROSS_SURFACES = False\n","print(\"G28203_STRONG_COUPLING_UNIFORMLY_BOUNDED_ACROSS_SURFACES =\", G28203_STRONG_COUPLING_UNIFORMLY_BOUNDED_ACROSS_SURFACES)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"81b9b9fc","metadata":{"id":"81b9b9fc"},"source":["# 8 — Reduced Dirac interpretation of the interface channel\n","\n","Away from the two surfaces, the compact-interface candidate carries one extra radial propagating channel. On the surfaces, the radial kinetic rank drops and the channel disappears. The question is whether this can be represented by a globally constant canonical class.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"id":"7dae7c3c","metadata":{"id":"7dae7c3c","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1787859904244,"user_tz":300,"elapsed":36,"user":{"displayName":"charlemagne oreste Laurince","userId":"04059779535451209712"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":230},"outputId":"66a39860-7372-4fe8-948b-fa903be36383"},"outputs":[{"output_